Welcome to Term49C!

Term49C ("C" = Classic) is a BlackBerry 10 terminal
emulator tuned for the BlackBerry Classic (Q20) hardware
— physical keyboard, trackpad, and belt keys — while still
usable on other BB10 devices. It continues Term48/Term49.

This file is linked into your home directory on first
launch. Topics:

1. QUICK START
2. CLASSIC HARDWARE (trackpad, belt keys)
3. MOUSE, SCROLLBACK, COPY/PASTE
4. SHIFT+TAB AND KEY TABLES
5. PREFERENCES
6. WHAT'S INSTALLED
7. SOURCE / HELP

===========================================================

1. QUICK START

Special keys (Ctrl, Alt, arrows, etc.) via metamode:
touch the top-left corner of the screen, then press a
key. A green 'M' appears top-right while metamode is on.
Touch the corner again to leave metamode.

Default metamode keys:

  h: left arrow      j: down arrow
  k: up arrow        l: right arrow
  t: tab             e: escape
  c: control         a: alt
  v: paste           s: rescreen

Arrow keys stay in metamode so you can move repeatedly.
Other keys exit metamode after one use.

Example: Ctrl-C — touch top-left (metamode), 'c' (ctrl),
then 'c' again.

On a physical keyboard you can also:
  - hold Space to toggle metamode (reliable on Classic)
  - hold letter keys for uppercase (keyhold_actions)

Double-tap Shift is optional and device-dependent. The default
is double-tap *right* Shift (metamode_doubletap_key =
KEYCODE_RIGHT_SHIFT). On the BlackBerry Classic (Q20) that
does **not** work: the hardware does not deliver a distinct
right-Shift event the way Term49C expects. Use hold-Space or
the top-left hitbox on Classic instead. On other devices (or
Bluetooth keyboards that send right Shift) double-tap may work;
you can also set metamode_doubletap_key to left Shift if your
keyboard only reports that key.

On the Classic, prefer the trackpad for arrows and the
Menu belt key for persistent Alt (see below).

===========================================================

2. CLASSIC HARDWARE (trackpad, belt keys)

TRACKPAD
  Swipe: arrow keys (history, cursor, vi/less, etc.).
  DECCKM application cursor mode is respected.
  Click: Enter by default (term info "kent").

  Settings in ~/.term49rc:
    trackpad_enabled = true;
    trackpad_sensitivity = 60;   /* lower = more keys/swipe */
    trackpad_click_keys = "kent"; /* "" disables click */

BELT KEYS
  Back: sends Esc (configurable: back_button_keys).
  Menu (BlackBerry key): toggles *persistent* Alt mode —
    every key uses the alt table; Alt+trackpad scroll is
    armed. Indicator 'a' shows while active. Hardware Alt
    remains one-shot. Swipe-down-from-bezel does the same.
  Send / End: keep system behaviour.

===========================================================

3. MOUSE, SCROLLBACK, COPY/PASTE

MOUSE (xterm reporting: DECSET 9/1000/1002/1003, SGR 1006)
When an app enables mouse tracking (tmux mouse, vim
set mouse=a, htop, mc, ...):

  - Trackpad drives a mouse pointer (inverse '+'); click
    is left button. When tracking ends, trackpad returns
    to arrow keys automatically.
  - Touch a cell to click; drag for motion (e.g. select
    in vim).
  - Alt + trackpad: wheel events (app scroll) instead of
    local scrollback.

SCROLLBACK (scrollback_lines, default 500)
  - Touch-drag up/down on the screen
  - Alt + trackpad swipe up/down
  Inverse '▲' top-right while scrolled back. Typing or
  trackpad arrows snaps to the live screen. Alternate-
  screen apps (less, vim) are unaffected.

COPY / PASTE
  - Copy: hold Alt (or Menu's persistent Alt), then drag
    across the screen. Release copies to the system
    clipboard. Tap clears selection.
  - Paste: metamode 'v' (or paste_clipboard). Bracketed
    paste (DECSET 2004) is supported when the app enables
    it.
  - OSC 52: remote programs can set the phone clipboard
    (e.g. tmux set-clipboard). Clipboard *reads* via
    OSC 52 are ignored for privacy.

CJK / DOUBLE-WIDTH
  East-Asian wide characters take two columns. Extra
  system fonts (Hei, MSung, malgun) fill Han/kana/Hangul
  gaps. See font_path, fallback_font_path, cjk_font_path.

===========================================================

4. SHIFT+TAB AND KEY TABLES

With Shift held or sticky shift armed (↑ indicator):
  - Virtual keyboard Tab → back-tab (ESC [ Z)
  - Metamode / sym / alt keys bound to Tab also send
    back-tab
  - Uppercase metamode bindings win when Shift is active
    e.g. ("T", "...") alongside ("t", "\t")

===========================================================

5. PREFERENCES

File: ~/.term49rc (libconfig syntax). Created with
defaults on first launch if missing. Errors fall back
to compiled defaults.

Selected options and Term49C defaults:

font_path = "/usr/fonts/font_repository/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf";
fallback_font_path = "../app/native/fonts/CascadiaMonoPL-Regular.ttf";
/* Glyphs missing from the main font (box drawing, braille,
 * powerline, ...) use the fallback. Set "" to disable. */

cjk_font_path = "/usr/fonts/font_repository/monotype/MHeiM.GB18030_200910.ttf";
/* Primary CJK face; additional system faces are chained
 * for kana/Hangul. */

font_size = 20;
text_color = [255, 255, 255];
background_color = [0, 0, 0];
screen_idle_awake = false;
auto_show_vkb = true;

metamode_doubletap_key = 61666;     /* KEYCODE_RIGHT_SHIFT — not useful on Classic Q20 */
metamode_doubletap_delay = 500000000;
keyhold_actions = true;
keyhold_actions_exempt = [KEYCODE_BACKSPACE, KEYCODE_RETURN];
metamode_hold_key = 32;             /* Space */
tty_encoding = "UTF-8";
metamode_hitbox : { x = 0; y = 0; w = 100; h = 100; };

metamode_keys : (
    ("e", "\x1B"),
    ("t", "\t")
  );
/* One-shot metamode → string, then exit metamode.
 * terminfo aliases: kcuu1, kcud1, kcuf1, kcub1, khome,
 * kend, kf1..kf12. Hex: \xHH */

metamode_sticky_keys : (
    ("k", "kcuu1"),
    ("j", "kcud1"),
    ("l", "kcuf1"),
    ("h", "kcub1")
  );
/* Like metamode_keys but stay in metamode. */

metamode_func_keys : (
    ("a", "alt_down"),
    ("c", "ctrl_down"),
    ("s", "rescreen"),
    ("v", "paste_clipboard")
  );

main_symmenu : (
  (
    ("q", "\x1b"), ("w", "1"), ("e", "2"), ("r", "3"),
    ("t", "\t"), ("y", "<"), ("u", ">"), ("i", "\x03"),
    ("o", "^"), ("p", "%")
  ),
  (
    ("a", "~"), ("s", "4"), ("d", "5"), ("f", "6"),
    ("g", "\\"), ("h", "|"), ("j", "&"), ("k", "`"),
    ("l", "=")
  ),
  (
    ("0", "0"), ("z", "7"), ("x", "8"), ("c", "9"),
    ("v", "{"), ("b", "}"), ("n", "["), ("m", "]"),
    ("$", "\x1b[A")
  )
);
/* Sym menu: groups are rows bottom→top. */

sticky_sym_key = true;
sticky_shift_key = true;
sticky_alt_key = true;
allow_resize_columns = false;
rescreen_on_symmenu = true;

trackpad_enabled = true;
trackpad_sensitivity = 60;
trackpad_click_keys = "kent";
back_button_keys = "\x1b";
scrollback_lines = 500;

prefs_version = <int>
/* Bumped by the app when defaults change; usually leave alone. */

===========================================================

6. WHAT'S INSTALLED

Stock BB10 userland is sparse. You get basic file tools
(ls, less, mv, …), python, elvis (vi-like). Term49C also
bundles mksh (better Unicode shell), ssh, scp, sftp, and
ssh-keygen under the app private bin path.

===========================================================

7. SOURCE / HELP

Term49C is open source (SDL, freetype, libconfig, ICU,
xterm-style sequences). Project home:

  https://github.com/jxw1102/Term49C

Upstream lineage: BerryFarm/Term49, mordak/Term48.

Bugs, ideas, and pull requests welcome on GitHub.

Happy hacking!
